B.aBj=new A.my("Previously immunised","2 doses on days 0 and 3, by either route. 1-site ID (0.1 mL) or 1-site IM.","2 doses on days 0 and 3. ID 0.1 mL at 1 site, or IM 1 vial at 1 site.",!1)
B.aBg=new A.my("RIG in Category II","Not indicated, except in immunocompromised patients, where RIG/RMAb is indicated.","Not indicated. For an immunocompromised person, local infiltration of RIG in both Category II and Category III.",!1)
B.aBk=new A.my("Immunocompromised route","States RIG/RMAb is indicated in Category II; does not separately restrict the route.","Explicitly requires the complete vaccine course by the INTRAMUSCULAR route in both Category II and III.",!0)
B.aBf=new A.my("Repeat exposure","Re-exposure within 3 months of completing PEP: wound treatment only \u2014 neither vaccine nor RIG is needed.","For Category II and III, if repeat exposure occurs in the future, treat as previously immunised and follow the algorithm \u2014 i.e. 2 doses on days 0 and 3.",!0)
B.aBe=new A.my("RIG remainder","Does not need to be injected IM at a distance; may be fractionated for other patients with aseptic precautions.","Entire dose, or as much as anatomically feasible, infiltrated into or as close as possible to the wound while avoiding compartment syndrome.",!1)
B.aBo=new A.my("Previously vaccinated with suspected nerve exposure","Not addressed.","The treating physician may consider RIG infiltration.",!0)
B.aBl=new A.my("Rabies monoclonal antibodies","Human RMAb 3.33 IU/kg (potency 40 IU/mL); RMAb cocktail 40 IU/kg (potency 600 IU/mL). WHO 2018 encourages RMAb over RIG where available.","The poster algorithm addresses RIG dosage; it does not print RMAb doses.",!1)
