B.bMi=s(["Preoccupation with \u22651 perceived defect in appearance not observable or slight to others","Repetitive behaviours (mirror checking, grooming, skin picking, reassurance seeking) or mental acts (comparing) in response","Preoccupation causes clinically significant distress or impairment","Preoccupation is not better explained by concerns with body fat/weight in an eating disorder"],t.s)
B.bMj=s(["dextrose bolus","D10","2 mL/kg","hypoglycaemia","hypoglycemia","minibolus","mini bolus","glucose bolus","low blood sugar","neonatal hypoglycaemia","D10W","D25","D50","central line dextrose","peripheral dextrose","GIR","glucose infusion rate","IDM","infant of diabetic mother","LGA hypoglycemia","SGA hypoglycemia","glucagon","diazoxide","congenital hyperinsulinism"],t.s)
B.bzp=s(["During the first two weeks after the last menstrual period, egg follicles mature in the ovaries under the stimulus of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH), a hormone secreted by the pituitary gland in the brain.","High levels of the hormone estradiol, produced by the developing egg follicle, cause secretion of luteinizing hormone (LH), another hormone from the pituitary gland. LH triggers release of the egg from its follicle (ovulation).","For women with 28-day cycles, ovulation usually occurs on days 13 to 15."],t.s)
B.er=s([],t.BS)
B.cRm=new A.fr("1&2","WEEKS 1 AND 2",1,null,B.bzp,B.er)
B.bwX=s(["During the third week, if fertilization occurs, the fertilized egg (zygote) begins producing the hormone human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG, the pregnancy hormone).","hCG first becomes detectable in the mother's blood and urine between 6 and 14 days after fertilization (3 to 4 weeks gestational age).","During the 3rd week the sex of the fetus is determined by the father's sperm, and twins may be formed.","Fatigue and swollen or tender breasts are sometimes the first signs of pregnancy."],t.s)
B.cR4=new A.fr("3","WEEK 3 \u2014 Embryonic age 1 week",1,null,B.bwX,B.er)
B.bNZ=s(["The embryo is approximately the size of a pinhead. Most pregnancy tests are positive at this time."],t.s)
B.cRq=new A.fr("4","WEEK 4 \u2014 Embryonic age 2 weeks \u2014 0.9 months",1,"Approximately the size of a pinhead",B.bNZ,B.er)
B.bDb=s(["The brain, spine, and heart have begun to form.","By the end of the week the heart will be pumping blood.","Week 5 is the beginning of the embryonic period, which lasts from the 5th to the 10th week.","It is during this critical period that many birth defects occur in the developing embryo. Most of these birth defects will have no known cause or will be due to a combination of factors (multifactorial)."],t.s)
B.J7=new A.IW(0,"critical")
B.cFg=new A.iL(B.J7,"START OF EMBRYONIC PERIOD (Weeks 5\u201310): Critical period for birth defects. Most major organ systems are forming during this time.")
B.bO9=s([B.cFg],t.BS)
B.cRf=new A.fr("5","WEEK 5 \u2014 Embryonic age 3 weeks \u2014 1.2 months",1,null,B.bDb,B.bO9)
B.bOw=s(["The embryo is now about the size of a pea.","The average crown\u2013rump length is about 0.2 inches (0.5 cm).","The eyes, nostrils, and arms are taking shape.","The heart is beating at about 110 beats per minute and sometimes may be seen using a transvaginal ultrasound at this time."],t.s)
B.cRg=new A.fr("6","WEEK 6 \u2014 Embryonic age 4 weeks \u2014 1.4 months",1,"About the size of a pea (average CRL ~0.5 cm / 0.2 inches)",B.bOw,B.er)
B.bOJ=s(["The embryo is now about 0.37 inches (0.95 cm) long.","The hands and feet are forming, as well as the mouth and face.","The heart is beating at about 120 beats per minute. Movement of the embryo can be detected by ultrasound.","By week 7 the trachea and bronchi of the lungs have formed, and the pseudoglandular stage of lung development begins.","Crown\u2013rump length of 7 mm or greater and no heartbeat, or mean sac diameter of 25 mm or greater and no embryo is considered consistent with early pregnancy loss."],t.s)
B.mG=new A.IW(1,"lung")
B.cF9=new A.iL(B.mG,"Pseudoglandular stage of lung development begins at week 7.")
B.mH=new A.IW(3,"warning")
B.cFd=new A.iL(B.mH,"CRL \u22657 mm with no heartbeat OR mean sac diameter \u226525 mm with no embryo = consistent with early pregnancy loss.")
B.bOp=s([B.cF9,B.cFd],t.BS)
B.cRp=new A.fr("7","WEEK 7 \u2014 Embryonic age 5 weeks \u2014 1.6 months",1,"~0.95 cm (0.37 inches)",B.bOJ,B.bOp)
B.bxQ=s(["The average embryo at 8 weeks is 0.6 inches (1.6 cm) long.","The embryo is about the size of a bean. The fingers and toes are developing.","The adrenal glands begin DHEA-S secretion and the testes begin to secrete testosterone.","In a process called physiological gut herniation, the intestine elongates and moves outside the abdomen into the base of the umbilical cord and rotates counter-clockwise at about 8 weeks. The intestine returns into the fetal abdomen by about 12 weeks."],t.s)
B.cRo=new A.fr("8","WEEK 8 \u2014 Embryonic age 6 weeks \u2014 1.8 months",1,"~1.6 cm (0.6 inches) \u2014 size of a bean",B.bxQ,B.er)
B.bQ3=s(["The heart is beating at about 170 beats per minute.","The average embryo at 9 weeks is 0.9 inches (2.3 cm) long."],t.s)
B.cR2=new A.fr("9","WEEK 9 \u2014 Embryonic age 7 weeks \u2014 2.1 months",1,"~2.3 cm (0.9 inches)",B.bQ3,B.er)
B.bR7=s(["The embryo's tail has disappeared and it is now called a fetus. Fingerprints are being formed, and bone cells are replacing cartilage.","The adrenal glands are starting to produce catecholamines and the pituitary is starting to release ADH and oxytocin.","The fetus can make IgM.","The average fetus at 10 weeks is 1.22 inches (3.1 cm) long and weighs about 1.2 ounces (35 grams)."],t.s)
B.cR3=new A.fr("10","WEEK 10 \u2014 Fetal age 8 weeks \u2014 2.3 months",1,"~3.1 cm (1.22 inches), ~35 grams",B.bR7,B.er)
B.bQK=s(["The fetus is starting to have breathing movements. It can open its mouth and swallow.","The average fetus at 11 weeks is 1.6 inches (4.1 cm) long and weighs about 1.6 ounces (45 grams)."],t.s)
B.cRa=new A.fr("11","WEEK 11 \u2014 Fetal age 9 weeks \u2014 2.5 months",1,"~4.1 cm (1.6 inches), ~45 grams",B.bQK,B.er)
B.bwc=s(["The fetus is starting to make random movements.","The fetus begins to concentrate iodine in its thyroid and produce thyroid hormone at about this time.","The pancreas is beginning to make insulin, and the kidneys are producing urine. The heartbeat can usually be heard with an electronic monitor at this time.","Experimental data suggest that human fetuses are capable of limited IgG synthesis by ~12 weeks' gestation. However, IgG present in the fetal circulation consist almost entirely of maternally derived IgG transported across the placenta.","The average fetus at 12 weeks is 2.1 inches (5.4 cm) long and weighs about 2.1 ounces (58 grams)."],t.s)
B.cR6=new A.fr("12","WEEK 12 \u2014 Fetal age 10 weeks \u2014 2.8 months",1,"~5.4 cm (2.1 inches), ~58 grams",B.bwc,B.er)
B.bLj=s(["The average fetus at 13 weeks is 2.6 inches (6.7 cm) long and weighs about 2.6 ounces (73 grams).","All major organs are formed now, but they are too immature for the fetus to survive out of the womb.","Physiologic gut herniation should be complete by this time.","The fetal bladder can consistently be seen using ultrasound after 13 weeks."],t.s)
B.cF2=new A.iL(B.J7,"END OF FIRST TRIMESTER")
B.bAc=s([B.cF2],t.BS)
B.cRj=new A.fr("13","WEEK 13 \u2014 Fetal age 12 weeks \u2014 3 months",1,"~6.7 cm (2.6 inches), ~73 grams",B.bLj,B.bAc)
B.bf5=s(["The fetus's toenails are appearing. The gender may sometimes be seen.","The average fetus at 14 weeks is 5.8 inches (14.7 cm) long (crown to heel) and weighs 3.3 ounces (93 grams)."],t.s)
B.cE_=new A.IW(4,"note")
B.cF7=new A.iL(B.cE_,"START OF SECOND TRIMESTER")
B.bEo=s([B.cF7],t.BS)
B.cR_=new A.fr("14","WEEK 14 \u2014 Fetal age 12 weeks \u2014 3.2 months \u2014 START 2ND TRIMESTER",2,"~14.7 cm crown to heel (5.8 inches), ~93 grams",B.bf5,B.bEo)
B.bN6=s(["Fetal movement may be sensed now (called quickening). Some mothers don't feel the fetus moving until about 25 weeks.","The average fetus at 15 weeks is 6.6 inches (16.7 cm) long and weighs 4.1 ounces (117 grams)."],t.s)
B.cRt=new A.fr("15","WEEK 15 \u2014 Fetal age 13 weeks \u2014 3.5 months",2,"~16.7 cm (6.6 inches), ~117 grams",B.bN6,B.er)
B.bxn=s(["The average 16-week fetus is 7.3 inches (18.6 cm) long and weighs 5.2 ounces (146 grams).","Hearing is beginning to form.","The pancreas begins to produce exocrine enzymes.","The canalicular period of lung development has started and will continue until about 25 weeks.","The average 17-week fetus is 8 inches (20.4 cm) long and weighs 6.4 ounces (181 grams).","The pseudoglandular stage of lung development ends at about 17 weeks. There are still no alveoli (the air sacs in the lungs where the exchange of oxygen and carbon dioxide occurs), so respiration is not possible at this time."],t.s)
B.cF5=new A.iL(B.mG,"Canalicular period of lung development begins ~16 weeks and continues to ~25 weeks. Pseudoglandular stage ends at ~17 weeks \u2014 no alveoli yet, respiration not possible.")
B.bNy=s([B.cF5],t.BS)
B.cRl=new A.fr("16","WEEKS 16\u201317 \u2014 Fetal age 14\u201315 weeks \u2014 3.7 to 3.9 months",2,"Week 16: ~18.6 cm (7.3 in), ~146 g  |  Week 17: ~20.4 cm (8 in), ~181 g",B.bxn,B.bNy)
B.bo_=s(["The ears are standing out, and the fetus is beginning to respond to sound.","The average 18-week fetus is 8.7 inches (22.2 cm) long and weighs 7.9 ounces (223 grams).","The thyroid becomes fully functional at 18 to 20 weeks.","The cerebellar vermis can be demonstrated to be fully formed on ultrasound at this age."],t.s)
B.cR8=new A.fr("18","WEEK 18 \u2014 Fetal age 16 weeks \u2014 4.1 months",2,"~22.2 cm (8.7 inches), ~223 grams",B.bo_,B.er)
B.bvF=s(["The ears, nose, and lips are now recognizable.","The average fetus at 19 weeks is 9.5 inches (24 cm) long and weighs 9.6 ounces (273 grams)."],t.s)
B.cRi=new A.fr("19","WEEK 19 \u2014 Fetal age 17 weeks \u2014 4.4 months",2,"~24 cm (9.5 inches), ~273 grams",B.bvF,B.er)
B.byO=s(["The fetus is covered in fine hair (lanugo), has some scalp hair, and is capable of producing IgG and IgM (two types of antibodies).","The parathyroid begins to regulate calcium metabolism.","The adrenal are starting to produce significant levels of cortisol.","The average fetus at 20 weeks is 10.1 inches (25.7 cm) long and weighs 11.7 ounces (331 grams)."],t.s)
B.cF1=new A.iL(B.mG,"HALFWAY POINT \u2014 20 weeks")
B.bNM=s([B.cF1],t.BS)
B.cRh=new A.fr("20","WEEK 20 \u2014 Fetal age 18 weeks \u2014 4.6 months",2,"~25.7 cm (10.1 inches), ~331 grams",B.byO,B.bNM)
B.bMw=s(["The fetus is now able to suck and grasp, and may have bouts of hiccups. Some women may begin feeling Braxton Hicks contractions at this time.","The average fetus at 21 weeks is 10.8 inches (27.4 cm) long and weighs 14.1 ounces (399 grams)."],t.s)
B.cRn=new A.fr("21","WEEK 21 \u2014 Fetal age 19 weeks \u2014 4.8 months",2,"~27.4 cm (10.8 inches), ~399 grams",B.bMw,B.er)
B.bMp=s(["The average fetus at 22 weeks is 11.4 inches (29 cm) long and weighs 1.1 pounds (478 grams)."],t.s)
B.cRr=new A.fr("22","WEEK 22 \u2014 Fetal age 20 weeks \u2014 5.1 months",2,"~29 cm (11.4 inches), ~478 grams",B.bMp,B.er)
B.bHH=s(["The fetus is having rapid eye movements during sleep.","The average fetus at 23 weeks is 12.1 inches (30.6 cm) long and weighs 1.3 pounds (568 grams).","The entire corpus callosum may not be seen using transabdominal ultrasound before this age."],t.s)
B.cFa=new A.iL(B.mH,"Approaching viability threshold \u2014 ~23 weeks")
B.bCa=s([B.cFa],t.BS)
B.cRd=new A.fr("23","WEEK 23 \u2014 Fetal age 21 weeks \u2014 5.3 months",2,"~30.6 cm (12.1 inches), ~568 grams",B.bHH,B.bCa)
B.bPN=s(["The average fetus at 24 weeks is 12.7 inches (32.2 cm) long and weighs 1.5 pounds (670 grams).","The terminal saccular stage of lung development has started."],t.s)
B.cFc=new A.iL(B.mH,"VIABILITY THRESHOLD \u2014 24 weeks")
B.cFi=new A.iL(B.mG,"Terminal saccular stage of lung development begins at 24 weeks.")
B.bx6=s([B.cFc,B.cFi],t.BS)
B.cR1=new A.fr("24","WEEK 24 \u2014 Fetal age 22 weeks \u2014 5.5 months",2,"~32.2 cm (12.7 inches), ~670 grams",B.bPN,B.bx6)
B.bJl=s(["The average fetus at 25 weeks is 13.3 inches (33.7 cm) long and weighs 1.7 pounds (785 grams).","The canalicular period of lung development is ending. Respiration is possible towards the end of this period."],t.s)
B.cF8=new A.iL(B.mG,"Canalicular period ending \u2014 respiration becoming possible towards end of 25 weeks.")
B.bIj=s([B.cF8],t.BS)
B.cRk=new A.fr("25","WEEK 25 \u2014 Fetal age 23 weeks \u2014 5.8 months",2,"~33.7 cm (13.3 inches), ~785 grams",B.bJl,B.bIj)
B.bT7=s(["The fetus can respond to sounds that occur in the mother's surroundings. Its eyelids can open and close.","The average fetus at 26 weeks is 13.8 inches (35.1 cm) long and weighs about 2 pounds (913 grams).","Survival out of the womb at this age would be expected to be approximately 87%."],t.s)
B.cR0=new A.fr("26","WEEK 26 \u2014 Fetal age 24 weeks \u2014 6 months",2,"~35.1 cm (13.8 inches), ~913 grams",B.bT7,B.er)
B.b8W=s(["The average fetus at 27 weeks is 14.4 inches (36.6 cm) long and weighs 2.3 pounds (1055 grams).",u.df],t.s)
B.cR5=new A.fr("27","WEEK 27 \u2014 Fetal age 25 weeks \u2014 6.2 months",2,"~36.6 cm (14.4 inches), ~1055 grams",B.b8W,B.er)
B.bNv=s(["The fetus has eyelashes and its skin is red and covered with vernix caseosa, a waxy substance believed to act as a protective film with anti-infective and waterproofing properties.","The average fetus at 28 weeks is 14.9 inches (37.9 cm) long and weighs 2.7 pounds (1210 grams).",u.df],t.s)
B.cFf=new A.iL(B.mG,"START OF THIRD TRIMESTER \u2014 28 weeks")
B.bIk=s([B.cFf],t.BS)
B.cRe=new A.fr("28","WEEK 28 \u2014 Fetal age 26 weeks \u2014 6.4 months \u2014 START 3RD TRIMESTER",3,"~37.9 cm (14.9 inches), ~1210 grams",B.bNv,B.bIk)
B.bxI=s(["The average fetus at 29 weeks is 15.4 inches (39.2 cm) long and weighs 3 pounds (1379 grams).","The average fetus at 30 weeks is 16 inches (40.5 cm) long and weighs 3.4 pounds (1559 grams).","The average fetus at 31 weeks is 16.5 inches (41.8 cm) long and weighs 3.9 pounds (1751 grams)."],t.s)
B.cR7=new A.fr("29-31","WEEKS 29\u201331 \u2014 Fetal age 27\u201329 weeks \u2014 6.6 to 7.1 months",3,null,B.bxI,B.er)
B.bHx=s(["The fetus is forming muscle and storing body fat. If the fetus is a boy, his testicles are descending.","The average fetus at 32 weeks is 16.9 inches (43 cm) long and weighs 4.3 pounds (1953 grams).","The average fetus at 33 weeks is 17.3 inches (44 cm) long and weighs 4.8 pounds (2162 grams).","The distal femoral epiphysis ossification center can usually be seen in about 72% of fetuses at 33 weeks."],t.s)
B.A3=new A.IW(2,"bone")
B.cF4=new A.iL(B.A3,"Distal femoral epiphysis ossification center visible in ~72% of fetuses at 33 weeks.")
B.bBr=s([B.cF4],t.BS)
B.cR9=new A.fr("32-33","WEEKS 32\u201333 \u2014 Fetal age 30\u201331 weeks \u2014 7.4 to 7.6 months",3,"Week 32: ~43 cm (16.9 in), ~1953 g  |  Week 33: ~44 cm (17.3 in), ~2162 g",B.bHx,B.bBr)
B.bM5=s(["The fetus is now considered to be late preterm.","The average 34-week fetus is 17.8 inches (45.2 cm) long and weighs 5.2 pounds (2377 grams).","The average 35-week fetus is 18.2 inches (46.3 cm) long and weighs 5.7 pounds (2595 grams).","The proximal tibial epiphysis ossification center may be seen in about 35% of fetuses at 35 weeks.","The average 36-week fetus is 18.6 inches (47.3 cm) long and weighs 6.2 pounds (2813 grams)."],t.s)
B.cFe=new A.iL(B.A3,"Proximal tibial epiphysis ossification center visible in ~35% of fetuses at 35 weeks.")
B.cFb=new A.iL(B.mH,"LATE PRETERM (34\u201336 weeks)")
